{"action":"final","query":{"op":"none","id":null,"start":null,"end":null,"search":null,"groupBy":null},"diagnosis":"getLiveIntervals follows descriptor views but stops at arith.select, so backing allocations can expire before the selected descriptor's last use. In case-24/25, the temporary occupies columns [0,64), overlapping both selected candidates; selected outputs become 7 (fact-24/26). With a 32-column temporary, only choice=1 fails (case-27, fact-29), while choice=0 passes (case-26, fact-27). Early allocation passes with disjoint storage (case-30, fact-33/34). The repair follows select results transitively alongside views and deduplicates traversal, covering chained and reconvergent selections. It retains interval-based reclamation, first-fit placement, alignment, row constraints, and layout behavior. Legal reuse in the direct-first control (case-32, fact-36/37) remains unchanged. Static IR supports premature storage reuse but does not establish hardware timestamps. No compilation or post-repair execution was available; repair success is not experimentally verified.","locations":[{"source_id":"source-01","start_line":120,"end_line":135},{"source_id":"source-02","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-03","start_line":15,"end_line":24},{"source_id":"source-06","start_line":16,"end_line":22}],"evidence_ids":["case-24","case-25","fact-24","fact-25","fact-26","case-26","case-27","fact-27","fact-28","fact-29","case-30","fact-33","fact-34","case-32","fact-36","fact-37","case-36","fact-42","fact-43"],"edits":[{"old":"  // Merge the alloc liverange with the liverange of any subview of the
